      "message": "I apologize for the initial approach. The first `led_pins` node label was a bit of a hack on my end (and Keith pointed it out). Seeing a second `led_pins2` node label now just confirms that we need a better solution.\n\nMy suggestion is:\n\nWe should introduce a new `led-pins` property in the policy node. This design will enforce a limitation: all color nodes under the same policy must reference the same `led-pins` configuration.\n\nI believe this is a reasonable constraint, as I haven\u0027t seen any feature request of the mixed use (`gpio-pins` and `pwm-pins` under the same policy) and don\u0027t foresee any potential use that would violate it.\n\nAs a result, this will also make a much clearer API design, each policy node just  points to one set of APIs; we don\u0027t need to embedded the APIs in every `led_pins_node_t` (http://crrev.com/c/7152689).\n\nLet me know what you think!",
